WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.840
Jute is a plant fiber
that spun into strong,

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.080
coarse twine for
traditional Basque

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.480
espadrilles. They use
twine that's about a 10th

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.500
of an inch thick.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.180
Large jute spools feed
an automated braiding

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.060
machine. Its five
bobbins move in a

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.540
circular pattern that
produces a neat braid,

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.010
measuring roughly three
fourths of an inch wide

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.210
by a quarter of an inch
thick.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.410
Right after exiting the
braiding machine, the

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.570
braid enters a
calibration machine,

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.970
which applies tension to
make the dimensions

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:38.300
uniform. Each espadrille
sole is handcrafted by an

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.780
artisan. He winds the
braid on a form that's

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.550
more than a century old.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.640
The positioning of the
metal pegs in the holes

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.790
correspond to the size
of the shoe he's making.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.670
The closer the pegs are
to each other, the

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.260
smaller the shoe size.

